gahM(){return"column"},
gahG(){return"This symbol isn't the right one for this cell. Change it."},
gahH(){return"These three identical symbols in a row (tinted cells) aren't allowed, and this one is one too many. Change it."},
ahF(a,b,c){return"This "+a+" has too many "+b+" (tinted cells): it only takes "+c+". This one is one too many. Change it."},
ahD(a,b){return"Two "+a+" side by side (tinted cells): adding a third would make three in a row, which isn't allowed. Place "+b+" here."},
ahE(a,b){return"This cell has "+a+" on each side (tinted cells): putting the same one here would make three in a row. Place "+b+" here."},
ahB(a,b,c,d){return"This "+a+" already has its "+b+" "+c+" (tinted cells): it can't have more, so all its empty cells take the other symbol. Place "+d+" here."},
ahC(a,b){return"Look at this "+a+" (tinted). Trying every way to complete it, with as many suns as moons and never three identical in a row, this cell always gets the same symbol. Place "+b+"."},
ahz(a,b,c){return"Try it: if this cell held "+a+", chaining deductions line by line would lead to this "+b+" (tinted), which could no longer be filled. So place "+c+" here."},
ahA(a){return"No simple reasoning applies right now. Place "+a+" here."},
ganF(){return"row"},
ganE(){return"column"},
ganA(){return"This cell is filled by mistake: it isn't part of the picture. Empty it."},
anB(a,b){return"The clue of this "+a+" ("+b+") makes this cell necessarily empty, yet it is filled. Empty it."},
ganC(){return"This cell is crossed off by mistake: it is part of the picture. Remove the cross."},
anD(a,b){return"The clue of this "+a+" ("+b+") makes this cell necessarily filled, yet it is crossed off. Remove the cross."},
anv(a,b){return"This "+a+" already has all its blocks ("+b+"): every cell left is empty. Cross them off."},
anw(a,b){return"This "+a+" has exactly as many cells left as its blocks ("+b+") need: every free cell is filled. Fill them."},
anz(a,b,c,d){return"In this "+a+" (clue "+b+"), the block of "+c+" can only slide by "+d+" cells, so wherever it sits it covers its middle cells: they are necessarily filled. Fill them."},
any(a,b){return"Look at this "+a+" (clue "+b+"). Trying every position of the blocks that fits what is already known of the line, these cells are always filled. Fill them."},
anx(a,b){return"Look at this "+a+" (clue "+b+"). Trying every position of the blocks that fits what is already known of the line, these cells are never covered. Cross them off."},
ganq(){return"Chaining the deductions of several rows and columns, including cells you haven't crossed off yet, this cell is necessarily filled. Fill it."},
ans(a){return"Try it: if this cell were empty, deductions line by line would lead to this "+a+" (tinted), which could no longer be filled according to its clue. So this cell is filled. Fill it."},
anr(a){return"Try it: if this cell were filled, deductions line by line would lead to this "+a+" (tinted), which could no longer be filled according to its clue. So this cell is empty. Cross it off."},
ganu(){return"No simple reasoning applies right now. This cell is filled."},
gant(){return"No simple reasoning applies right now. This cell is empty."},
gXN(){return"horizontal (wider than tall)"},
gXP(){return"vertical (taller than wide)"},
gXO(){return"a square"},
XK(a,b){return"This rectangle has "+a+" cells, but the number it holds is "+b+": its area must equal that number. Erase it."},
gXM(){return"A rectangle must hold exactly one number: this one holds none, or several. Erase it."},
XL(a){return"This rectangle is well formed, but with it the tinted "+a+" has nowhere left to go. Erase it."},
gXJ(){return"This rectangle is well formed, but it isn't part of the solution: it stops the rest of the grid from being covered by the other numbers. Erase it."},
XI(a){var s=""+a
return"The tinted "+s+" has only one possible rectangle: it's the only one of "+s+" cells that holds it without touching another number or a rectangle already drawn. Draw the tinted area."},
XF(a){return"No other number can reach the circled cell: only the tinted "+a+" can cover it. Just one of its rectangles holds it: draw the tinted area."},
XE(a){return"Chaining several cells only one number can cover, the tinted "+a+" is left with a single possible rectangle. Draw the tinted area."},
XH(a,b){return"The rectangle of the tinted "+a+" is "+b+". The mark stays on the number and helps with what follows."},
XG(a){return"No simple deduction is left, even with the shapes. Here is the rectangle of the "+a+": draw the tinted area."},
an_(a){return"The line of "+a+" leads nowhere: whatever you do next, the grid can no longer be filled. Go back to the circled cell and erase what follows (tinted area)."},
amY(a){return"This end of "+a+" has only one free cell to go to. Extend the line over the tinted area."},
amW(a){return"From this end of "+a+", any other way would leave the shaded cell without enough free neighbors: a cell must be crossed by a line, so it needs two neighbors. Only one way is left: extend the line over the tinted area."},
amZ(a){return"From this end of "+a+", every other way leads, a few cells on, to a grid that can't be filled. Only this one works: extend the line over the tinted area."},
amX(a){return"Several ways are still possible from this end of "+a+". Here is one that leads to a complete grid: extend the line over the tinted area."},
gX9(){return"The path starts on the 1 (circled cell). Put your finger on it, then drag."},
gXa(){return"This path can't succeed: it will no longer be possible to go through every cell, in the order of the numbers. Go back to the circled cell and erase what follows (tinted area)."},
gX7(){return"From the head of the path there is only one cell to go to: the others are already taken, or carry a number that isn't the next one. Move on to the tinted area."},
gX4(){return"Any other neighboring cell would cut the grid in two: the shaded cell could no longer be reached. Move on to the tinted area."},
gX5(){return"Any other neighboring cell would leave the shaded cell with a single free neighbor: you could only enter it to get stuck, while the path must go on. Move on to the tinted area."},
gX8(){return"Any other neighboring cell leads, a few cells on, to a grid that can't be finished. Only this one works: move on to the tinted area."},
gX6(){return"Several cells are still possible for now. Here is the continuation of a path that reaches the end: move on to the tinted area."},
